    {
      "kind": "struct",
      "name": "UnsafeBodyNoRef",
      "ty_idx": 113,
      "type_params": [
        "T"
      ],
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "forceInline",
          "ty_idx": 16
        }
      ],
      "description": "`UnsafeBodyNoRef` is used to prevent default behavior: when message body is potentially large,\nit's packed into a separate ref. Wrapping body with this struct tells the compiler:\n\"inline message body in-place, I guarantee it will fit\".\n```\nstruct ProbablyLarge { a: (coins, coins, coins, coins, coins) }\n\nval contents: ProbablyLarge = { ... };  // you are sure: values are small\ncreateMessage({\n    // body: contents,           // by default, will be a ref (max 620 bits)\n    body: UnsafeBodyNoRef {\n        forceInline: contents,   // but it forces the compiler to inline it\n    }\n```\nAnother example: your body contains `builder` or `RemainingBitsAndRefs`: unpredictable size.\nIf you guarantee it's small and refs won't clash with code/data, avoid creating a cell."
    },
